Verne 6.8.0
===========

The first release of Verne, a GTK4 + libadwaita presentation of Nemo, based on
Nemo 6.7.5. See debian/changelog for the full list of changes, README.md for
what Verne is and is not, and THANKS for credit to the projects it is built on.

Highlights:

- The user interface is ported from GTK3 to GTK4 and libadwaita. Nemo's
  internal APIs, D-Bus names, GSettings schemas, extensions and actions are
  unchanged, so Nemo actions and extensions keep working.

- The whole window follows the desktop's light/dark preference. Previously the
  chrome, the icon view, the rubber band and the properties-window capacity
  ring were painted with fixed light colours.

- Menu rows read label-left / accelerator-right again, with a real check mark
  and submenu arrows.

- The places-sidebar free-space indicator works again, deriving its colours
  from the theme rather than from GTK3 widget style properties that GTK4
  removed.

- Icons that came from Mint's xapp-symbolic-icons now resolve on any system.


Development: 1/22/2013:

- Breadcrumbs:  Stylable by themes, see src/nemo-styles-fallback.css for default style information.
                Border radius, color, background color, and text color can be customized through that.

- Sidebar Disk Indicators:  Stylable by themes, again, see src/nemo-styles-fallback.css for default
                style information - you can customize the two colors (fore- and background), the
                thickness of the bar, the corner radius, the maximum length of the bar, and an amount
                of extra padding from the bottom of the cell.
